# Side by Side brand rules

Design reference: `reference/prototype.html` (approved). When in doubt, copy it.

## Colours (tokens in src/styles/tokens.css)
- --night #0B161D (page ground), --ink #13232E (surfaces, primary), --ink2 #1A2F3C
- --paper #F4F6F3 (text on dark, light sections), --mist #D7DEDB, --slate #52616B, --muted #9AAAB2
- --mari #F0B429 (the one accent), --mari-d #8A5E08 (accent text on light)
- Marigold is never body text on light grounds. Text on marigold is always ink.
- Site is dark-first with light (paper) and marigold sections for rhythm. No gradients except the subtle ones already in the prototype.

## Type
- Commissioner (variable, Greek subset) for everything readable. Display weight 800, tight tracking (-0.035em to -0.055em). Weight 200 for "thin" words in headlines.
- JetBrains Mono for eyebrows, labels, chips, metadata: uppercase, letter-spacing .1–.14em.

## Logo and motif
- Mark: two vertical bars, lead bar paper/ink, second bar marigold offset one step lower. Never level the bars, never swap colours.
- The offset bar pair is the motif: eyebrow marker, button icon, menu button, footer "side ∥ side".
- Logo SVGs in reference/*.svg.

## Copy
- Greek, monotonic, first person singular («εγώ»), addressing the client in singular («σου»).
- Clear, calm, direct. Short sentences. Numbers over adjectives.
- Never mention "junior". Never speak badly of agencies (they are clients too).
- Never show prices on the site. Use durations or billing model ("6–8 εβδομάδες", "ανά έργο", "μηνιαία", "με την ώρα").
- No em dashes in running text, no emoji, no exclamation marks.

## Motion
- Every animation from the prototype is part of the brand. Keep easing cubic-bezier(.2,.8,.2,1).
- Respect prefers-reduced-motion everywhere. Scroll-driven CSS behind @supports ((animation-timeline: view()) and (animation-range: entry)).
- Content must be readable without JS.
